Checkers registered for ``For`` and ``With`` now also run on ``async for`` and
``async with``. The AST walker dispatches on the node's exact class name, so
``visit_for`` never received an ``AsyncFor`` even though ``AsyncFor`` is a
subclass of ``For``. This makes ``useless-else-on-loop``,
``confusing-with-statement``, ``redeclared-assigned-name`` and
``redefined-argument-from-local`` fire on the async forms.

``unnecessary-dict-index-lookup``, ``unnecessary-list-index-lookup`` and
``unbalanced-dict-unpacking`` also reach their ``async for`` handler now, but
all three need to infer a dict, a list or ``enumerate()`` as the iterated
object, which cannot be an async iterator in valid code, so in practice they
only apply to code that is already broken.

Closes #11417
